# ============================================================================
# FlowSpecies / isobaric contact between two gases of different gamma, advected  (species.eos = mixture, stage 2a)
#
# Gas A (gamma 1.4, c_v 2.5) in 0.25 < x < 0.75, gas B (gamma 5/3, c_v 1.5) outside; p = 1, u = 1, rho = 1 in A and
# 0.5 in B; periodic, one pass (t = 1).  Exact: pressure and velocity stay uniform and the profile returns to its start.
# A conservative scheme does NOT keep the pressure uniform across a contact where gamma changes (Abgrall 1996): this
# test MEASURES that error, max |p - p_0| / p_0, against resolution.  It is the number that decides when a gas | gas
# interface should be modelled with two phases (which keep it uniform) instead of two species of one phase.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 4 ./hydro2-2d-g++ ../tests/FlowSpecies/input_1D_IsobaricSpeciesContact plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           python3 ../tests/FlowSpecies/reference/two_gamma_check.py contact <dir> [<dir> ...]
# ============================================================================
plot_file = ./tests/FlowSpecies/output_1D_IsobaricSpeciesContact
amr.plot_dt = 0.25
